        "caption": "Charles at Penrhyn Castle. Charles is a saddle tank locomotive which has close connections with Penrhyn. Charles was one of the 'main line' engines used at Penrhyn Quarry. Built by Hunslet Engine Co of Leeds in 1882, Charles worked until the 1950s and after restoration was placed on permanent loan to the National Trust.",
